  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of comprehensive service-offers designed and rolled out to support SDG financing

2. Number of UNDP COs guided on the implementation of SDG finance-related innovative tools and services  

3. Volume (USD) of financial resources mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG financing

4. Number of expert rosters established to broaden and deepen expertise on SDG financing

5. Number of internal stakeholders trained on SDG finance-related tools, products, services

6. Number of high-level events (UNGA, HLPF) hosted to promote and advance SDG financing

7. Number of online knowledge platforms launched to promote and advance SDG financing

8. Number of technical specialists and experts available to guide regional and country work</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. No comprehensive service-offers available to support SDG financing

2. 15 COs receive limited guidance the implementation of SDG finance-related innovative tools and services 

3. 0 USD mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG financing

4. No expert rosters exist to broaden and deepen expertise on SDG financing

5. Limited number of internal stakeholders trained on Islamic Finance private-sector engagement for SDGs  

6. 10 high-level events hosted in Y2018 to promote and advance SDG financing

7. 5 online knowledge platforms available to promote and advance private-sector engagement for SDGs

8.  4 technical specialists available to guide regional and country work on private-sector engagement for SDGs</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Mapping of existing tools and services completed

2. 50 COs guided on the implementation of SDG-finance related innovative tools and services

3. At least USD 15 M mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG financing

4. At least 2 expert rosters initiated

6. At least 10 high-level events hosted to promote and advance SDG financing

7. At least 7 online knowledge platforms operational to promote and advance SDG financing

8. Available BPPS technical positions aligned with FSH matrix and new project capacities established</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 100+ tools and services mapped

2. 70 COs guided on the implementation of SDG-finance related innovative tools and services (IICPSD, BCtA, CBi, INFF, TIWB)

3. USD15.9 M mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG Financing (CIG, GDF, TIWB, SDGI, IICPSD, CBi, INFF)

4. INFF expert roster launched, TIWB expert roster is being finalized

6. 20 high-level events hosted and supported to promote and advance SDG financing (BCtA, CBi, SDGPP, TIWB, GDF, INFF)

7. 8 online platforms operational to promote and advance SDG financing (IICPSD, SDGPP, CBi, BCtA, GIFIIP, SDG Impact, TIWB and SFH)

8. 4 BPPS regional positions aligned with SFH matrix and recruitment of 5 project specialists underway</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Existing and new tools, services and approaches mapped and clustered 

2. At least 80 COs guided on the implementation of SDG-finance related innovative tools and services

3. At least USD 15 M mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG financing

4. At least 2 experts rosters available for use by COs

6. At least 10 high-level events hosted to promote and advance SDG financing

7. At least 10 online knowledge platforms operational to promote and advance SDG financing

8. At least 10 technical specialists and experts available to guide regional and country work</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 128 tools and services mapped, reviewed, and clustered for further development of comprehensive service offers

2. 80+ COs guided on the implementation of SDG-finance related innovative tools and services (IICPSD, BCtA, CBi, INFF, TIWB, SDGI, IRFF)

3. USD 30 M mobilized for UNDP in support of SDG Financing (GDF, TIWB, IRFF, SDGI, CBi, BCtA, INFF, SFH)

4. INFF and TIWB experts rosters operationalized via GPN ExpRes Roster; Bond / Debt Financing expert roster initiated.

6. 20+ high-level events hosted and supported to promote and advance SDG financing (SFH, BCtA, CBi, SDGPP, TIWB, GDF, INFF, SDGI, IRFF)

7. 10 online platforms operational to promote and advance SDG financing (IICPSD, SDGPP, CBi, BCtA, GIFIIP, SDG Impact, TIWB, SFH, INFF and IRFF)

8. 18 technical specialists and experts available to guide regional and country work (CBi, SFH, TIWB, IRFF, SDGI)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
